# What the build context must not carry. Not a tidiness measure: the host's
# node_modules is a pnpm tree full of absolute symlinks into a store that does
# not exist in the image, so copying it in produces a build that resolves to
# nothing. The images install their own.
#
# Every pattern is anchored with `**/`, which is not decoration either: Docker
# matches these against the path from the context root, so a bare `node_modules/`
# excludes the root one only. Checked rather than assumed — with the bare form,
# `apps/backend/node_modules`, `apps/frontend/.next` and `packages/core/dist` were
# all still in the context, and the Dockerfiles copy those directories whole.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/dist/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/next-env.d.ts

# Never in an image, at any depth, and never only at the root: an app's
# `.env.production` is the file that most wants to be a secret. `.env.example` is
# the tracked template and is the one exception — it carries no secret and
# documents the rest.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# The dev SSH keypair the runner presents to the sshd fixture, and the fixture
# itself. Neither belongs in a production image.
infra/sshd/keys/
infra/terraform/

.git/
.github/
**/coverage/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
**/.vitest/
docs/
e2e/
**/*.md
